<section id="world" aria-labelledby="worldtitle"><h2 id="worldtitle">Explore world libraries</h2><p class="subhead">Ten established research, reading and language-study resources. Some provide freely readable books; others provide listening, borrowing, original-language tools, or searchable archives.</p><div class="cards"><article class="source-card"><div class="eyebrow">Books and historical theology</div><h3>Project Gutenberg</h3><p>Catalog of digitized books, including classic works on theology.</p><p class="tags">Languages: Many languages</p><p class="rights">Free online reading; EPUB/text; U.S. rights labels do not decide Mexico or other-country copyright</p><a class="visit" href="https://www.gutenberg.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Explore resource ↗</a></article><article class="source-card"><div class="eyebrow">Christian classics</div><h3>Christian Classics Ethereal Library</h3><p>Read classic Christian texts; special editions and introductions can have distinct rights.</p><p class="tags">Languages: Primarily English</p><p class="rights">Free reading; redistribution of CCEL editions requires separate review</p><a class="visit" href="https://www.ccel.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Explore resource ↗</a></article><article class="source-card"><div class="eyebrow">Academic theological archives</div><h3>Princeton Theological Commons</h3><p>Historical books, journals, sermons, manuscripts, and archival resources.</p><p class="tags">Languages: Multiple languages</p><p class="rights">Free access; item-level rights vary</p><a class="visit" href="https://commons.ptsem.edu/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Explore resource ↗</a></article><article class="source-card"><div class="eyebrow">Modern course books</div><h3>Shepherds Global Classroom</h3><p>Biblical and practical ministry course textbooks and audio.</p><p class="tags">Languages: English; separate Spanish collection</p><p class="rights">Publisher-specific reuse conditions; books must stay intact</p><a class="visit" href="https://courses.shepherdsglobal.org/downloads/english" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Explore resource ↗</a></article><article class="source-card"><div class="eyebrow">Bible commentaries</div><h3>Free Bible Commentary</h3><p>Bob Utley’s exegetical resources for Bible study.</p><p class="tags">Languages: Many languages including Swahili</p><p class="rights">Free online PDFs/audio; inspect attribution and embedded Bible rights</p><a class="visit" href="https://www.freebiblecommentary.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Explore resource ↗</a></article><article class="source-card"><div class="eyebrow">Biblical languages and text study</div><h3>STEP Bible</h3><p>Compare Bible texts and explore original Hebrew and Greek.</p><p class="tags">Languages: Multilingual</p><p class="rights">Free online tool; text/translation licenses vary</p><a class="visit" href="https://www.stepbible.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Explore resource ↗</a></article><article class="source-card"><div class="eyebrow">Lectures and courses</div><h3>BiblicalTraining</h3><p>Audio teaching by Christian academics; not a hosted-book collection.</p><p class="tags">Languages: Primarily English</p><p class="rights">Free listening to classes; certificate programs may cost</p><a class="visit" href="https://www.biblicaltraining.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Explore resource ↗</a></article><article class="source-card"><div class="eyebrow">Digitized academic books</div><h3>HathiTrust Digital Library</h3><p>Large library consortium with older theological publications.</p><p class="tags">Languages: Multiple languages</p><p class="rights">Some full view, some search only; geographical restrictions</p><a class="visit" href="https://www.hathitrust.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Explore resource ↗</a></article><article class="source-card"><div class="eyebrow">Books and lending</div><h3>Open Library</h3><p>Search and borrow digitized library books; availability varies by title.</p><p class="tags">Languages: Multiple languages</p><p class="rights">Some titles borrowable with account; not free redistribution</p><a class="visit" href="https://openlibrary.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Explore resource ↗</a></article><article class="source-card"><div class="eyebrow">Historic books and media</div><h3>Internet Archive</h3><p>Search historical theological books, periodicals and audiovisual resources.</p><p class="tags">Languages: Multiple languages</p><p class="rights">Mixture of public-domain, borrowable, and restricted items</p><a class="visit" href="https://archive.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Explore resource ↗</a></article></div></section>
<section id="rights" class="policy"><h2>How CTS can use these resources</h2><ol><li><strong>Linking:</strong> this preview links directly to official provider pages; it does not store external book files, replace CTS's existing required-reading rooms, or alter examinations.</li><li><strong>Project Gutenberg:</strong> its catalog labels these particular editions public domain in the United States. Publication or translation by a Mexico-based seminary requires separate local and edition-specific analysis. See <a href="https://www.gutenberg.org/about/background/free_ebook.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Gutenberg's explanation</a>.</li><li><strong>CCEL:</strong> historic base texts may be public domain, while introductions and editions can have separate restrictions. CCEL asks users to seek permission to republish its prepared works. <a href="https://www.ccel.org/about/copyright.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read its policy</a>.</li><li><strong>Modern publisher books:</strong> Shepherds Global Classroom specifies conditions for distributing an intact work; this does not automatically authorize adaptations or translations. <a href="https://shepherdsglobal.org/copyright/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Publisher policy</a>.</li><li><strong>Academic selection:</strong> inclusion means potentially useful for study, not agreement with every historical, denominational or theological assertion. Faculty must assess relevance and quality before titles are endorsed or assigned.</li></ol><p><strong>Next editorial step:</strong> faculty review the list, then approved entries can be connected to courses and languages without changing existing course completion rules.</p></section></main>
